<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ansfried of Utrecht</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1010</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ansfried was a count in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> who served Emperor Otto III before becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Utrecht in 995. Around 990 he and his wife Hilsondis founded the convent of Thorn, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>, with their daughter Benedicta as its first abbess. Going blind in later life, he retired to the abbey of Hohorst, which he had founded, and died there in 1010. He is venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ansfried-of-utrecht.jpg" alt="Ansfried of Utrecht" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huy_051027_(38).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
